  "_about": "Chenonceau: the white tuffeau of the Loire in fine ashlar on every wall, blue-grey slate on every roof, cone and dormer hip, lead on the roof's flat and the finials; the piers, the bridge and the terrace walls in coursed stone, the Tour des Marques' older masonry greyer under its white top; inside, the vestibule flagged, the rooms in terracotta tiles, the gallery's lower floor a diagonal chequer of black and white, its upper floor oak, timber ceilings.",
